  "versionNotes": [
    {
      "edition": "C# 12 to C# 13 ref-struct locals in async methods",
      "items": [
        "Before C# 13, async methods could not declare ref-struct locals. Starting with C# 13, ref-struct locals are allowed when they are not used across an await suspension boundary. This language relaxation does not make Span<T> heap-storable or allow it to survive suspension."
      ],
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/csharp/whats-new/csharp-13",
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/csharp/language-reference/builtin-types/ref-struct"
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": ".NET 5-11 memory and diagnostics additions",
      "items": [
        "The `pinned` parameter on `GC.AllocateArray<T>` and `GC.AllocateUninitializedArray<T>` enables POH allocation for supported arrays; `GC.AllocateArray<T>(pinned: true)` was added in .NET 5. .NET 11 `dotnet-gcdump` supports blocking buffering to reduce event loss for large heap captures. These additions do not change Span<T> and Memory<T> ownership or lifetime rules."
      ],
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.gc.allocatearray",
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.gc.allocateuninitializedarray",
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/diagnostics/dotnet-gcdump"
      ]
    }
