  "accuracyFacts": [
    "Before C# 13, async methods could not declare ref-struct locals. C# 13 permits them only when they are not used across an await suspension boundary; they remain non-heap-storable.",
    "Span<T>, ReadOnlySpan<T>, Memory<T>, and ReadOnlyMemory<T> CopyTo operations throw when the destination is shorter than the source, not when lengths merely differ; overlapping ranges are supported.",
    "The TryCopyTo methods return false without writing when the destination is too short; overlapping ranges are supported.",
    "Memory<T> and ReadOnlyMemory<T> are views and do not transfer ownership or extend the backing storage lifetime."
